# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Environment / secrets
# Unlike the private security-tooling-dev repo, .env.op is NOT committed here.
# It holds only op:// references, never values — but this repository is public,
# and a reference still names a vault and an item. See docs/adr/0003.
.env.op
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem

# Real hunt output never belongs in a public repository. Only the sanitised
# worked examples under examples/ are tracked. See docs/adr/0003.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: an unanchored `hunts/` matches at
# EVERY level, so it also swallowed examples/hunts/ and silently kept the worked
# example out of the repository. Caught by the second-AI review, and now by
# tests/test_examples.py.
/hunts/

# macOS / editors
.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Skill evaluation runs: generated transcripts, outputs and benchmarks. Kept on
# disk so iteration N can be compared against N-1, kept out of git because they
# are large, regenerable, and not part of the skill.
/threat-hunt-workspace/
